<svg class="hidden h-auto w-full lg:block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 960 496" role="img" aria-labelledby="pitch-title" aria-describedby="pitch-desc" font-family="Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif">
  <title id="pitch-title">How Deploybot lets AI agents run your servers</title>
  <desc id="pitch-desc">People use the web console in a browser. Any MCP client, such as a coding agent, a chat app or your own script, connects to Deploybot over MCP, signed in as you. Deploybot acts with your project role, runs only what your catalog allows, and asks for a confirm step. Deploybot itself is hosted or self-hosted. Your servers run bot-agent, which dials out to Deploybot, so no ports are open. The agent never gets SSH keys or cloud tokens for the servers.</desc>
